# Production signing material -- NEVER commit these to git.
#
# key.properties holds plaintext keystore/key passwords, and *.jks/*.p12/
# *.keystore are the actual private signing key. In this project both are
# provisioned only:
#   - locally, by a developer copying their own securely-held keystore in, or
#   - in CI, by the "Decode signing key" step in
#     .github/workflows/flutter-build.yml, which reconstructs them at build
#     time from GitHub Actions repository secrets and never persists them
#     back into the repository.
key.properties
app/*.jks
app/*.keystore
app/*.p12

# Exception: app/shared-debug.keystore is NOT production signing material --
# it is a plain, non-secret, self-signed DEBUG-only key (see build.gradle's
# signingConfigs.debug), committed deliberately so every build (local or CI)
# signs with the SAME debug key. Without this, CI's ephemeral runners would
# each have Android Gradle Plugin auto-generate a brand-new, random debug
# keystore on every run, making consecutive CI-built APKs mutually
# upgrade-INCOMPATIBLE whenever no production key is configured (confirmed:
# two consecutive runs produced different SHA-256 signer fingerprints before
# this file existed). Its password ("android") and alias ("androiddebugkey")
# are the well-known, non-secret Android debug-keystore conventions.
!app/shared-debug.keystore
